  "what_the_count_is": "Every `count` in this file is a count of PRINTED LABELS located on the sheet, not a count of building members. The 138 labels recorded here are 138 marks drawn on three sheets. One framing line can carry two labels, one label can cover several members, and R.R.1 labels a framing zone rather than a rafter — which is why each entry states `counted` and why a reading that reports members is recorded as counting something else, never as being wrong.",
  "how_to_check_an_entry": "These sheets carry a 270-degree rotation, so the renderer draws each one landscape at ~200 dpi: 7196 x 4794 px, cut into a 2x2 grid (each tile 3598 x 2397 px) plus a whole-page overview. Open the tile named in `tiles` and look at the page coordinates in `places`. Every label can be found that way; nothing here rests on a number without a place.",
  "page_numbering": "`page` and `tiles` are numbered for the standalone three-sheet file used for this comparison, where S-2 is page 1, S-3 page 2 and S-4 page 3. `page_in_submittal_set` is the same sheet's page in the full 30-page set."
}
